> API and interpretation

Dont-cares may help form a prime but need not be covered. Required/optional
duplicates normalize, and overlapping assignments remain required. The hard
representable variable count is0..32, avoiding shifts by32; the default policy
allows16. The zero-variable true function has one empty-literal product, whereas
an empty required set has an empty cover. Only truth assignments in the declared
domain are accepted. The report prints cube strings and actual chart ids; no
report-local minimization or covering search is used.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Quine, The Problem of Simplifying Truth Functions (1952)|https://doi.org/10.1080/00029890.1952.11988183]
- [McCluskey, Minimization of Boolean Functions (1956)|https://doi.org/10.1002/j.1538-7305.1956.tb03835.x]

